Ours.  Declarations gcc 14 needs in the X libraries and their headers (X11, Xi, Xp, Xmu, Xaw, ICE, SM, xtrans, include/):
each file that called a function with no declaration gets a prototype after its
includes, taken from the definition the call links with (gcc -aux-info).  A K&R
definition's narrow parameters are default-promoted in the prototype, as a K&R caller
passes them (char/short/their typedefs -> int, float -> double):
  lib/X11/imCallbk.c: _XimError(CARD16 error_code -> int); _XimError(INT16 detail_length -> int); _XimError(CARD16 type -> int)
  lib/X11/imDefLkup.c: _XimError(CARD16 error_code -> int); _XimError(INT16 detail_length -> int); _XimError(CARD16 type -> int)
  lib/X11/imTransR.c: _XimError(CARD16 error_code -> int); _XimError(INT16 detail_length -> int); _XimError(CARD16 type -> int)
  lib/font/Type1/scanfont.c: objFormatReal(float value -> double); objFormatBoolean(boolean value -> int)
  lib/font/bitmap/bdfread.c: bdfSpecialProperty(char isString -> int)
Declared without a prototype (types not defined at that point, or called with varying
arguments; none has an ANSI definition with a narrow parameter): +extern int 
(*XESetCloseDisplay())();	/* Xlibint.h's, unprototyped */ _IceTransClose 
_X11TransFreeConnInfo _XDisconnectDisplay XkbApplyVirtualModChanges 
_XrmInternalStringToQuark 
Headers whose macros call a function get a declaration beside the macro: 
include/extensions/extutil.h lib/Xaw/XawI18n.h lib/xtrans/Xtrans.h 
Also: NULL as a character in lcGeneric.c and omGeneric.c becomes '\0' (and 0 for 
memset): <stdlib.h> makes NULL (void *)0.

